糟了
No!

344
00:13:12,420 --> 00:13:12,860
糟了
Oh, no.

345
00:13:13,420 --> 00:13:14,640
尼玛
Oh, hell no.

346
00:13:16,980 --> 00:13:18,680
好吧 等等 爸 我们得想个借口
Okay. Wait, wait, Dad. We need an excuse!

347
00:13:18,680 --> 00:13:20,361
人们会奇怪我们怎么没睡的
People are gonna wonder why we weren't in bed.

348
00:13:20,729 --> 00:13:22,132
告诉他们...
Um, tell them that, uh, uh...

349
00:13:22,480 --> 00:13:24,680
我们在阳台是因为我看到了一头驼鹿
Oh! We were on the balcony because we saw a moose.

350
00:13:24,920 --> 00:13:25,540
太蠢了
That's dumb.

351
00:13:26,100 --> 00:13:27,860
告诉他们我在厨房给你热牛奶
We'll tell them I'm heating up some milk for you in the kitchen

352
00:13:27,860 --> 00:13:29,060
因为你胃疼
because your stomach hurts.

353
00:13:29,440 --> 00:13:31,560
为什么 因为我看到驼鹿吓到了吗
Why? Because I was upset that I saw a moose?

354
00:13:36,500 --> 00:13:37,720
快穿上
Put this on.

355
00:13:38,800 --> 00:13:40,240
-我扔早了 -我接晚了
- I was early. - I was late.

356
00:13:42,740 --> 00:13:43,500
快 快
Hurry, hurry!

357
00:13:44,660 --> 00:13:46,960
你身上还是有很重的大象味
I'm still getting strong notes of elephant off of you.

358
00:13:47,560 --> 00:13:49,360
-你搞不好得把头发都剪了 -不要
- You may have to cut off all your hair. - No!

359
00:13:51,180 --> 00:13:53,560
我知道大家都很好奇我为什么叫你们来
I'm sure you're wondering why I've gathered you all here.

360
00:13:53,680 --> 00:13:56,018
小皇冠裂了 你在短信里说了
Uh, the tiara's cracked. You told us in your text.

361
00:13:56,018 --> 00:13:57,860
但我没告诉你们 我发誓
What I didn't tell you is that I've vowed

362
00:13:57,860 --> 00:13:59,280
要找出是谁干的
to find out who's responsible.

363
00:13:59,540 --> 00:14:01,100
不 其实你说了 短信很长...
Well, no, actually, you did. It was a fairly long --

364
00:14:01,540 --> 00:14:03,160
所有人都有嫌疑
Everyone's a suspect.

365
00:14:03,440 --> 00:14:05,120
别看我 我根本没靠近过小皇冠
Don't look at me. I wasn't anywhere near it.

366
00:14:05,240 --> 00:14:07,440
"真意外" 菲尔装无辜
What a surprise -- Phil feigning innocence.

367
00:14:07,780 --> 00:14:09,580
人人都最喜欢你这个憨厚老爸是吧
You're just everyone's favorite Dad, right?

368
00:14:09,820 --> 00:14:11,340
收到我短信时你在哪
Where were you when you got my text?

369
00:14:12,060 --> 00:14:13,840
小卡他 胃疼
Cam's, uh, stomach was upset,

370
00:14:13,840 --> 00:14:15,640
我在帮他热牛奶
and I was warming up some milk for him.

371
00:14:16,340 --> 00:14:17,680
-克莱尔看到一头驼鹿 -是的
- Claire saw a moose. - ?I did.

372
00:14:17,920 --> 00:14:20,860
所以收到短信时我们在阳台上
And that's why we were on the balcony when you texted us.

373
00:14:21,320 --> 00:14:22,500
歌洛莉亚和我在活动室
Well, Gloria and I were in the den.

374
00:14:22,540 --> 00:14:24,120
我出去散步时偶遇她
I ran into her on my way out to my walk,

375
00:14:24,120 --> 00:14:25,700
然后我们决定一起赏月
and then we decided to watch the moon together.

376
00:14:25,880 --> 00:14:26,600
赏月是吗
The moon, huh?

377
00:14:26,628 --> 00:14:29,495
不太可能吧 因为今晚没有月亮
Seems unlikely given tonight is moonless!

378
00:14:30,340 --> 00:14:31,200
没关系
No matter.

379
00:14:32,380 --> 00:14:35,260
那你们有没有人经过这间房间
So, did any of you go through this room at any point?

380
00:14:36,640 --> 00:14:39,600
在我听来所有人都在室内
Sounds to me like everybody was inside

381
00:14:39,600 --> 00:14:40,980
做他们在做的事
doing whatever they were supposed to be doing.

382
00:14:41,300 --> 00:14:44,160
那就怪了 因为我发现这扇门没关严
That's odd because I found this door slightly open,

383
00:14:44,160 --> 00:14:45,940
那意味着你们有人出去了
which means one of you was outside.

384
00:14:46,220 --> 00:14:47,940
等我查出是谁从这扇门出去了
When I find out who went out that door,

385
00:14:48,440 --> 00:14:49,460
我很肯定他就是犯人
quite sure I'll have my culprit.

386
00:14:49,920 --> 00:14:50,880
那是什么
Hey, what's that?

387
00:14:53,380 --> 00:14:55,620
似乎是两个姜饼小人的下半身
It appears to be two bottom halves

388
00:14:55,620 --> 00:14:57,480
被融合在一起了
of a gingerbread man melded together.

389
00:14:57,480 --> 00:14:59,920
看起来像骨头 是块狗饼干
Uh, it looks like a bone. It's a dog treat.

390
00:15:00,080 --> 00:15:01,780
不 那是人吃的饼干
No, it's a human treat,

391
00:15:01,880 --> 00:15:04,640
做成骨头形状是因为富含钙质
and it's shaped like a bone because it's full of calcium.

392
00:15:04,820 --> 00:15:06,800
我之前在吃这些饼干
I was snacking on them earlier in the day

393
00:15:06,800 --> 00:15:08,440
肯定是掉了一块
and I must have dropped one.

394
00:15:10,948 --> 00:15:12,178
真好吃
Mmm, they're delicious.

395
00:15:13,000 --> 00:15:14,359
对身体还很有好处
And they're very good for you.

396
00:15:14,359 --> 00:15:15,546
说得通
Checks out.

397
00:15:16,700 --> 00:15:18,020
是楼上传来的
That's coming from upstairs!

398
00:15:18,200 --> 00:15:19,240
不 是外面
No, outside.

399
00:15:21,160 --> 00:15:22,880
歌洛莉亚 怎么会这样
Gloria, how did this happen?

400
00:15:23,040 --> 00:15:23,880
我有个理论
I have a theory.

401
00:15:24,240 --> 00:15:27,180
我有次读到过一头驼鹿把露营车给撞换挡了
I once read about a moose that knocked a camper out of neutral.

402
00:15:27,640 --> 00:15:30,260
或许克莱尔之前看到的驼鹿也那样做了
Perhaps the moose Claire saw earlier did the same thing here.

403
00:15:30,420 --> 00:15:32,760
-引擎盖还是热的 -那就别靠在上面
- The hood's warm. - Then don't lean on it.

404
00:15:33,080 --> 00:15:36,020
我承认 米奇和我之前在屋外
I admit it! Mitch and I -- we were outside.

405
00:15:36,380 --> 00:15:38,360
他想和我聊聊他和小卡
He wanted to talk to me about a problem

406
00:15:38,360 --> 00:15:41,200
在基佬卧室里不和谐的问题
he's having with Cam in the gay bedroom.

407
00:15:41,660 --> 00:15:42,960
这么说我不行就是有问题
Oh, so when it's me, it's a problem.

408
00:15:43,000 --> 00:15:44,900
你不行就是因为健身累的
When it's you, it's what happens when you work out too much.

409
00:15:45,100 --> 00:15:48,820
我们觉得冷 就坐进车里了
It got cold, we went inside the car,

410
00:15:48,820 --> 00:15:50,160
我打开了暖气
I turned the heater on,

411
00:15:50,160 --> 00:15:53,480
所以肯定是我不小心把车撞到了空挡
and I must have accidentally knocked it into neutral.

412
00:15:53,480 --> 00:15:55,800
所以驼鹿来的时候 车早已蓄势待滑
So, it was all ready to roll when the moose showed up.

413
00:15:56,000 --> 00:15:58,260
这个糖果盘怎么在这
Hey, uh, what's this candy dish doing here?

414
00:15:58,340 --> 00:15:59,700
海莉 拜托 我在思考
Haley, please, I'm trying to think.

415
00:15:59,880 --> 00:16:01,120
但那可能是证据
But it could be evidence.

416
00:16:01,220 --> 00:16:03,420
网球场的灯怎么亮着
What are the lights doing on in the tennis court?!

417
00:16:07,540 --> 00:16:09,340
这些椅子怎么会在这
Now why would these chairs be out here,

418
00:16:09,340 --> 00:16:10,660
这些又与驼鹿有什么联系
and how do they connect to the moose?

419
00:16:10,760 --> 00:16:13,840
这些脚印... 规律好奇怪啊
These footprints are in a... really weird pattern.

420
00:16:14,080 --> 00:16:16,062
为什么这步伐感觉如此熟悉
Why do these steps feel so familiar?

421
00:16:16,062 --> 00:16:17,271
我跟小卡来过这里
Cam and I were out here, um --

422
00:16:17,600 --> 00:16:20,640
我们本来在厨房 然后听到外面有浣熊的声音
We were in the kitchen, and we heard a raccoon outside.

423
00:16:20,720 --> 00:16:22,860
对啊对啊 所以我们出来了...
Yeah, yeah. So, we came out, we --

424
00:16:22,938 --> 00:16:25,410
我们拿了凳子来... 来吓走它
we grabbed a couple chairs to -- to -- to scare it off.

425
00:16:25,410 --> 00:16:27,474
我们这么... 这么拿着凳子
We held -- held them up like this,

426
00:16:27,727 --> 00:16:29,440
然后呢... 追着那浣熊
and, um, chased the raccoon,

427
00:16:29,440 --> 00:16:31,560
结果它跑进垃圾堆里 我们就...
but it ran into some trash cans and we were like...

428
00:16:32,533 --> 00:16:34,934
然后它跑到球场这里来
And then, uh, it ran up the court this way... ?

429
00:16:34,934 --> 00:16:36,497
然后又退了几步
...and then back a couple of steps

430
00:16:36,497 --> 00:16:37,915
-又再往前了一次 -往前
- and then forward again and - Forward.

431
00:16:37,915 --> 00:16:38,940
然后它最后转了一圈 往前跑
then it did a little spin. Forward, and

432
00:16:38,940 --> 00:16:39,900
对 就这样
Yep. That was it.

433
00:16:39,900 --> 00:16:41,780
接着它对我们冲过来 我们就
And then it came back at us, and we were like --

434
00:16:41,780 --> 00:16:44,028
右左 右 右
Right, left. Right, right,

435
00:16:44,028 --> 00:16:44,980
卷身 最后转
body roll, and spin.

436
00:16:44,980 --> 00:16:46,340
然后它就跑了
And then, it was just gone.

437
00:16:47,220 --> 00:16:48,260
刚才是什么玩意儿
What the hell was that?

438
00:16:48,340 --> 00:16:50,720
这是什么鬼 我完全无法理解这些线索
What is any of this? I can't make sense of these clues.

439
00:16:51,080 --> 00:16:53,280
哪有浣熊不会被巨大的驼鹿给吓跑啊
What kind of raccoon isn't scared off by the presence of a moose?

440
00:16:53,480 --> 00:16:54,600
我们只需要知道
All we need to know

441
00:16:54,600 --> 00:16:57,280
米奇尔 歌洛莉亚 小卡与菲尔
is that Mitchell, Gloria, Cam, and Phil

442
00:16:57,280 --> 00:17:00,460
-是唯四嫌疑人 -才不是唯四
- are the four and only suspects. - Not only!

443
00:17:01,900 --> 00:17:04,500
一个一个说 菲尔你先说
One at a time! Phil, go first.

444
00:17:04,620 --> 00:17:05,800
这样压力好大啊
Well, that's a lot of pressure.

445
00:17:06,000 --> 00:17:06,240
说
Speak!

446
00:17:07,260 --> 00:17:08,380
那什么声音
What is that noise?

447
00:17:08,720 --> 00:17:10,140
听起来像是一条狗在说"哈喽"
It's like a dog saying, "Hello."

448
00:17:10,340 --> 00:17:11,940
听起来像加州犬吠驼鹿的声音啊
Sounds to me like a California barking moose.

449
00:17:11,960 --> 00:17:12,900
从上面传来的
It came from up there.

450
00:17:16,496 --> 00:17:19,420
我们刚才讲解追浣熊的事时 好合拍啊
We were really in-sync talking through that raccoon chase.

451
00:17:19,420 --> 00:17:21,858
-感觉我们的拍子又重新合上了 -真的呢
- It felt like maybe we had our timing back again. - It really did.

452
00:17:21,858 --> 00:17:25,280
或许刚才我们忘了舞蹈不是为了名气或荣耀
Maybe we forgot dance isn't about the fame or -- or glory,

453
00:17:25,280 --> 00:17:28,160
而是用来对观众们诉说
but it's about telling a story that takes your audience

454
00:17:28,160 --> 00:17:30,280
一段跌宕起伏的故事
on a journey that ebbs and flows.

455
00:17:31,180 --> 00:17:31,548
跌宕起伏[艾博与弗洛/律动]
Ebb and Flow.

456
00:17:31,548 --> 00:17:34,021
我们的嘻哈诨名就是这个了
I think we just found our hip-hop names.

457
00:17:38,700 --> 00:17:39,220
杰
Jay!

458
00:17:39,720 --> 00:17:41,560
-你带斯黛拉来了吗 -没有啊
- You brought Stella?! ?- No!

459
00:17:41,560 --> 00:17:43,240
她自己跑来找我们了
She must have tracked us here.

460
00:17:43,600 --> 00:17:44,560
你说什么啊 小姑娘
What's that, girl?

461
00:17:45,360 --> 00:17:47,600
什么 家里的炉灶火没关吗
What? We left the stove on?

462
00:17:47,842 --> 00:17:49,620
-真是怪事 -等等 稍等一下
- Well, that was weird. - Wait, wait. Whoa, whoa.

463
00:17:49,620 --> 00:17:51,420
我的拖鞋为什么在这里面
What is my slipper doing in here?

464
00:17:51,420 --> 00:17:53,360
我没说错吧 的确是有些冷
I'm not wrong. It's cold, huh?

465
00:17:53,680 --> 00:17:55,420
亲爱的
Hey. Honey...

466
00:17:56,320 --> 00:17:58,260
我们得谈谈这件事
We need to talk about this. ?

467
00:17:58,280 --> 00:18:02,704
-斯黛拉 -她想要那个拖鞋啊 菲尔
- Um, Stella... - She wants the slipper, Phil.

468
00:18:02,704 --> 00:18:03,965
天啊
Oh, my God.

469
00:18:03,965 --> 00:18:06,400
为什么菲尔穿得像嘻哈男团的人
W-Why is Phil dressed like a Beastie Boy?

470
00:18:06,400 --> 00:18:07,399
等等 等等
Wait a minute. Wait a minute.

471
00:18:07,399 --> 00:18:10,417
你们俩个不带我们跳嘻哈
You two did hip-hop without us! ?

472
00:18:10,437 --> 00:18:12,420
是啦 因为你跟克莱尔是我们的累赘
Okay, be-because you and Claire were holding us back.

473
00:18:12,420 --> 00:18:14,419
少来了 我们跳得跟你们一样好
Oh, please. We are just as good as you are.

474
00:18:14,419 --> 00:18:16,639
-感觉有人想要来斗舞啊 -没有
- It sounds like somebody wants a dance-off. - No.

475
00:18:16,639 --> 00:18:18,460
永远不会有人想要斗舞
No one ever wants a dance-off.

476
00:18:18,460 --> 00:18:20,780
-菲尔 你为什么不直接跟我说 -省省吧 克莱尔
- Phil, why didn't you just tell me? - Save it, Claire.

477
00:18:20,820 --> 00:18:22,580
我知道是你对我的熊熊拖鞋搞鬼
I know you put the hit out on my bear slippers.

478
00:18:22,720 --> 00:18:24,457
这拖鞋很让人提不起性趣
Those are just very unsexy.

479
00:18:24,457 --> 00:18:27,040
难道你就整天穿得很性感吗
Oh, 'cause you always dress so sexy?

480
00:18:27,040 --> 00:18:28,720
来看看你今晚的睡衣
Let's check out this nightwear.

481
00:18:30,971 --> 00:18:32,340
卢克的初中体育课短裤
Luke's junior high gym shorts,

482
00:18:32,340 --> 00:18:33,900
而腰上的松紧带是用旧鞋带改的
and the drawstring is an old shoelace.

483
00:18:34,100 --> 00:18:35,880
至少我不是那种花大钱
Well, at least I'm not one of those wives

484
00:18:35,880 --> 00:18:37,440
在睡衣上面的那种败家老婆啊
that spends a fortune on lingerie.

485
00:18:37,540 --> 00:18:39,637
你看 这鞋带断掉的时候
I mean, look, when the shoelace broke,

486
00:18:39,637 --> 00:18:41,580
我用订书机修好了
I fixed it with a staple.

487
00:18:41,580 --> 00:18:43,680
我们度假时为什么就不能来点激情呢
Well, why don't we add a little spice for our vacation?

488
00:18:43,860 --> 00:18:46,580
歌洛莉亚就穿着及地的珠珠睡袍睡觉啊
I mean, Gloria wears a floor-length, beaded nightgown to bed.

489
00:18:46,680 --> 00:18:48,420
等等 她才没有呢
Wait a second. No, she doesn't.

490
00:18:50,940 --> 00:18:51,396
厉害了
Yes.

491
00:18:51,396 --> 00:18:53,940
它网站上的图片看起来很舒适啊
It looked very comfortable on the website.

492
00:18:53,940 --> 00:18:55,979
等一下 歌洛莉亚晚上跟米奇尔在一起
Wait a minute. Gloria was with Mitchell.

493
00:18:55,979 --> 00:18:57,427
我们看看这里面有何乾坤
What have we got going on under here?!

494
00:18:57,427 --> 00:18:59,180
你是想去哪里啊 穿这么衣冠楚楚
Okay, where were you going looking so dapper?!

495
00:18:59,180 --> 00:19:01,137
衣冠楚楚 真的吗
Dapper? Really? Aww...

496
00:19:01,708 --> 00:19:03,389
曼尼 曼尼
Oh! Ooh! Manny. Manny!

497
00:19:03,463 --> 00:19:06,380
看看米奇尔舅舅的口袋里掉出了什么
Hey! Look what just fell out of Uncle Mitch's pocket!

498
00:19:06,380 --> 00:19:08,040
第二个糖果盘...
A second candy dish...

499
00:19:08,140 --> 00:19:11,150
-等等 -这上面有刻字
- Hold up. - This is monogrammed.

500
00:19:11,150 --> 00:19:12,900
"M.O."
"M.O."?

501
00:19:12,900 --> 00:19:14,500
你没带我就去米歇尔·奥巴马家吗
You went to Michelle Obama's without me?

502
00:19:16,320 --> 00:19:18,080
你去奥普拉·温福瑞家没带我吗
You went to Oprah Winfrey's without me?!

503
00:19:18,960 --> 00:19:20,080
歌洛莉亚 这是真的吗
Gloria, is this true?

504
00:19:20,500 --> 00:19:22,900
你明明知道我对奥普拉有何感觉 她改变了我...
You know how I feel about Oprah. She changed my --

505
00:19:22,900 --> 00:19:23,500
我修正一下
Excuse me.

506
00:19:24,020 --> 00:19:26,200
她给了我改变自己人生的力量
She gave me the strength to change my own life!

507
00:19:26,540 --> 00:19:26,900
小卡
Cam.

508
00:19:31,320 --> 00:19:32,500
停下 停下
Stop. Stop!

509
00:19:32,620 --> 00:19:33,060
都停下
Stop!!

510
00:19:34,200 --> 00:19:36,280
我们忘记了重点是有人弄裂了
Have we all forgotten that somebody

511
00:19:36,280 --> 00:19:38,040
我老板的小皇冠吗
cracked my boss's tiara?!

512
00:19:38,140 --> 00:19:39,220
